This page is for anyone in the Lojban community who wants to help
the BPFK with the initial language description task.

Here's what you do:

* Log in to your account here; register if necessary (it's in the upper right)
* Make sure your email here is valid; see [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-user_preferences.php|the preferences page]
* Ignore anything else you've ever heard about BPFK procedures
* Pick a section that isn't green on the ((BPFK Sections)) page.  Pick a cmavo in that section that looks unfinished.  Do the following:
** Grab your CLL, or use one of the online versions.  Figure out what the cmavo means.  Write it down.  See the templates below.
*** Do ''NOT'' describe its category in general; it is sufficient to say that something is "an attitudinal"; you do not need to talk about how attitudinals in general work at all.
*** Do describe how it is different from other members of its category.
** Find (or, if you really can't find any, make) examples of usage of the cmavo; use the ((Corpora)) page for this.
** Search [http://groups.google.com/group/lojban|the mailing list], or anything else that seems relevant, for debate about the nature of the cmavo or its category.  Make notes of any you find, seperate from the body of the definition.

At any stage along the way, if you see any problem (contradictions, arguments, confusions, whatever) about either the cmavo itself ''or'' the general category it belongs to, make sure they are noted down, either in the Notes section for the cmavo or the Notes section (make one if necessary) for the whole page.

When editing the wiki, ''DO NOT WORRY'' about making mistakes or anything like that.  You are totally free to edit as you see fit.  This ''very much includes'' fixing other people's mistakes.  Edit as you see fit.  Do not discuss the page on the page; if there's something that needs discussion, post to [http://groups.google.com/group/bpfk-list|the BPFK group].  If a page is locked, let [http://groups.google.com/group/bpfk-list|the BPFK group] know.  We have people watching every edit; if there's a problem, we'll mail you.

Please put {...} around any cross-references to other Lojban words,
like {broda}. This will not get marked up, but it will save us a lot
of trouble later.

If you get stuck or confused, please post to [http://groups.google.com/group/bpfk-list|the BPFK group].

! Templates

A finished cmavo looks something like this:

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: xxx (SELMAHO)

!!! Proposed Definition

Attitudinal modifier. Used to express whatever.  

!! See Also

* {XYY}
* {XYZ}
* {GISMU}

!!! Proposed Keywords

* whatever
* shyeah-right!

!!! Usage Examples

;xxx mi klama:"Whatever!  I'm going."

!!! Notes

This cmavo is completely non-standard, but ''very'' common in actual usage.  We could resolve this by allowing it, or not.
{BOX}

The raw markup for that is this:

{BOX()}
~pp~
!! cmavo: xxx (SELMAHO)

!!! Proposed Definition
Attitudinal modifier. Used to express whatever.  

!! See Also
* {XYY}
* {XYZ}
* {GISMU}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* whatever
* shyeah-right!

!!! Usage Examples
;xxx mi klama:"Whatever!  I'm going."

!!! Notes
This cmavo is completely non-standard, but ''very'' common
in actual usage.  We could resolve this by allowing it, or not.
~/pp~
{BOX}
